{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Leticia can walk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0ee00a7e721afb0ad9bc07f27f8160f6516a2df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\text { km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b40b4e32530d70637864ee0dfa87d156a2b4cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text { minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. Walking at this same rate, how far does Leticia walk in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f760103c18c8860ecc479e0809779101b214953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\text { hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac52cca7258ea8e3da1f7f5d48e739987402ac92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 18 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 30 \\text{ km} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22.5 \\text { km} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 15 \\text { km} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4.5 \\text { km}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"556\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can convert <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168e597260a75c7dc7e69db9404d71c3ae383380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\text{ hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> into minutes. Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d315459dc283a3340c58a91ed9d09a1c8631185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec02e90ca8b96618fa3ad3a30f9beb8513a0b510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{hour}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168e597260a75c7dc7e69db9404d71c3ae383380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\text{ hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c3bfc03993dae3a16863dd5a96e4334617fba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60 \\times 4 = 240 \\text{ minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/3446888ad9747d582b6d2b17221a5fad8f1c9354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\text{minutes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> goes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d1058bad0159847f4edfc03a23d73eeeb4fc3121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\text{hours}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc74ff48b429a4378b5dde0eccbc7be11d1c40a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {240}{20} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" /> times.\n</p><p>This means that in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours, she travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf9c7d2f233319ebc42f60b421e8365a37d7f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 1.5 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 18 \\text{ km}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"183\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=